data.hypothesis:
Hand-built observables tie more directly to k than the raw readings do:
(a) temporal finite differences of log u, which are local decay rates and track the Rayleigh-quotient eigenvalue in k;
(b) differences of log u between adjacent sensors, which approximate log flux ratios across segments and so constrain k_i/k_{i+1};
(c) time-integrated temperature per sensor, which relates to the Green's function, scales like 1/k, and averages out noise.
The data layout is unknown, so both sensor-major and time-major reshapes are included. Kernel ridge on these features should recover k more sharply than on raw values.
